<title>USA: CME lumber closes mostly lower in quiet conditions.</title>
<headline>CME lumber closes mostly lower in quiet conditions.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>CME lumber futures closed mostly lower in thin volume as weakness in U.S. treasury bonds and U.S. stocks weighed on the market.</p>
<p>Dealers said the cash lumber market also remained weak.</p>
<p>Volume was light with both buying and selling interest scattered.</p>
<p>September lumber closed up $0.50 at $361.00 per thousand board feet with other months down $0.30 to $1.50.</p>
<p>((Nigel Hunt 312-408 8720))</p>
</text>
